  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tw_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -334
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Tile world\n\nA small island built in layers. Terrain: noise elevation on a 24 × 24 grid, falling off toward the edge, coloured by height (water, sand, grass, forest, rock, snow) and drawn as Cells — one square per tile, `colors` per cell. Roads: the Tiles node's wave function collapse lays edge-matched road tiles, masked to the land. Decorations: trees are a Symmetry rosette stamped on every forest tile, villages a kaleidoscope plaza on a few grass tiles. Clouds are metaballs (Contours' `points` mode) drifting with their shadows. A day/night cycle tints the world, and at night the villages light up.\n\n• Slider into `sea`: the sea level.  • Slider into `tod` + toggle: time of day / run the clock.\n• Vary: a new island and road network.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 270
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Tile world\n\nA small island built in layers. Terrain: noise elevation on a 24 × 24 grid, falling off toward the edge, coloured by height (water, sand, grass, forest, rock, snow) and drawn as Cells — one square per tile, `colors` per cell. Roads: the Tiles node's wave function collapse lays edge-matched road tiles, masked to the land. Decorations: trees are a Symmetry rosette stamped on every forest tile, villages a kaleidoscope plaza on a few grass tiles. Clouds are metaballs (Contours' `points` mode) drifting with their shadows. A day/night cycle tints the world, and at night the villages light up.\n\n• Slider into `sea`: the sea level.  • Slider into `tod` + toggle: time of day / run the clock.\n• Vary: a new island and road network.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
